  "peculiarities": "ஃ is called ஆய்தம் (aaytham). It is neither a soul letter nor a body letter: it stands on its own, between the two families.\n\nIt is a soft breath, a gentle 'hh' from the back of the throat. It never begins a word; it sits between a short vowel and a hard consonant, as in எஃகு (ekku, steel).\n\nIts shape is three dots, like three snakes curled up to rest. Some call it the 'third eye' letter.",
